  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know, the magnetic field on the axis of a current carrying circular ring is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></mrow></mfenced>